title: date_rosinante_4_Start
location: quarters
---

Today was such a long day, you think as you fall face-first into your bed. Not only did you have your regular workload to deal with, complete with Vice Admiral Tsuru's demands for perfection and high performance rate, but then Instructor Garp managed to rope you into helping him with his own paperwork—paperwork he had been avoiding for weeks, apparently.
The only bright part of the day was running into Rosinante during lunch. Of course, it meant more stress, as he had *somehow* managed to set his curry on fire... But that was the kind of stress you actually didn't mind dealing with for some reason. Instead, it charged you with energy to tackle the rest of the day—at least until Inspector General Sengoku's goat ate one of your reports and you had to redo the whole thing.
To this moment, you have no idea how the goat even managed to *find it* inside a closed drawer.
All in all... You're completely exhausted. Every single minute of this day was exhausting and right now, you want nothing more than to sleep for a week straight. You refuse to believe it's only Wednesday! How are you supposed to survive two more days of work before catching a break?!
Your eyes fall shut, and you don't fight it. You may not even have had dinner yet, but you don't even care anymore. You let darkness cover you like a blanket—
There's a knock on the door, snapping you awake.
{$name}: What is it *now...?*
-> Ignore it
    You should probably get up and find out what's going on...
    But, you can't say you *care* right now. Hell, you can barely even move. You doubt you have the capacity to deal with anything that doesn't involve a pillow and ten hours of absolutely *nothing.*
    With a sigh, you simply bury yourself deeper into your blanket and drift off to sleep, never finding out who was behind your door.
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_DATE_ENDS>>
-> Open the door
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_OPEN_DOOR>>
-> Tell them to come in
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_COME_IN>>
===

title: date_rosinante_4_OPEN_DOOR
location: quarters
---

For a moment, you play with the idea of ignoring whoever has decided to ruin your day even *further* but...
With a tired, long-suffering groan, you force yourself to get out of the comforting embrace of your bed. Not bothering to put on your slippers, you stumble barefoot towards the door.
The moment you open it, Rosinante, with his hand up in the air as if he was about to knock again, yelps and jumps up in surprise. You're a little proud of him when he manages to find his balance without falling on his butt.
{$name}: Rosinante? Are you OK?
Rosinante: {$name}, you scared me! I thought you weren't there.
You giggle at the way Rosinante's clutching at his heart. One would think you've dumped cold water on him out of nowhere.
{$name}: Sorry, I was in bed, almost asleep. What did you need?
Rosinante: Oh, I'm the one who's sorry! I didn't think I'd wake you up...
Rosinante: It's nothing important, you should rest.
You study Rosinante's expression for a moment; he's avoiding your gaze, looking sheepish. You can't tell if it's because he's feeling guilty for interrupting you or if it's because what he came for *was* important and now he feels awkward.
-> I'm sorry.
    {$name}: Can we talk later? I'm really tired right now...
    Rosinante: Of course, I didn't mean to wake you up.
    Rosinante: As I said, it's not important.
    Rosinante: Good night.
    As he walks away, his shoulders hunched up dejectedly, you feel a pang of guilt. Maybe you should have heard him out...
    But you can barely keep your eyes open. It's not like you'd be able to give him your full attention anyway!
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_DATE_ENDS>>
-> {$name}: No, it's OK!
    {$name}: Please, come in.
    Rosinante: Thank you.
    You ignore the way your heart flutters at the sight of his soft smile, instead stepping aside and opening the door wider, gesturing to Rosinante to come in.
    Suddenly, you realize there's a pile of clean clothes on your desk chair that you yet have to put where they belong, a few empty glass bottles that you keep forgetting to throw out, and several books and papers lying on the floor around your bed that you couldn't have been bothered to put away.
    You wince.
    {$name}: Sorry about the mess...
    Rosinante: You call this a mess? You should see my room.
    He chuckles as he passes you, and a smile tugs on your lips as you close the door.
    {$name}: You can sit on the bed, since the chair's—or wait, I'll just free up the chair. Sorry...
    Rosinante huffs as you hurry to grab the clothes occupying the chair, putting them on the desk instead.
    Nobody said you were good at panic cleaning!
    Taking a deep breath, you force yourself to calm down.
    Finally, you sit on your bed, facing Rosinante and giving him your full attention.
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_TALK_START>>
===

title: date_rosinante_4_COME_IN
location: quarters
---

For a moment, you play with the idea of ignoring whoever has decided to ruin your day even *further* but...
With a tired, long-suffering groan, you resign yourself to your fate. That doesn't mean you have to *move* though, does it?
{$name}: Door's open!
You don't even bother to look up when the door creaks open slowly—man, you really need to get those hinges oiled—and a person steps inside.
Rosinante: Should I... come by later?
It takes you a second to place the voice, but once you realize it's Rosinante, you turn your head to the side the smallest bit, cracking one eye open to glance at him.
He's standing at the door, one foot in and the other still out, clutching at the door and seemingly frozen in place at the sight of your half-dead body collapsed on the bed. His expression is twisted in worry and he looks so *guilty* to have interrupted you.
{$name}: Sorry, long day...
{$name}: What did you need?
Rosinante: I'm the one who's sorry! It's nothing important, I'll just let you rest.
As soon as he's done speaking, he steps away, about to leave the room, but the movement's hesitant. You study his face for a moment; he's avoiding your gaze, looking sheepish. You can't tell if it's because he's feeling guilty for interrupting you or if it's because what he came for *was* important and now he feels awkward.
-> I'm sorry.
    {$name}: Can we talk later? I'm really tired right now...
    Rosinante: Of course, I didn't mean to wake you up.
    Rosinante: As I said, it's not important.
    Rosinante: Good night.
    As he closes the door behind himself as quietly as he can, you catch one last glimpse of his dejected expression and a pang of guilt runs through you. Maybe you should have heard him out...
    But you can barely keep your eyes open. It's not like you'd be able to give him your full attention anyway!
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_DATE_ENDS1>>
-> It's OK.
    {$name}: Please come in.
    You ignore the way your heart flutters at the soft smile he gives you; instead, you force yourself to sit up straight in your bed, rubbing at your eyes to force them to stay open just a bit longer. When you look up again, Rosinante is standing awkwardly in the middle of your room as if not sure what to do with himself.
    {$name}: Rosinante? You OK?
    Rosinante jumps at your words and it feels like he doesn't know how to say what's on his mind.
    Rosinante: Uhm...
    Rosinante: Where—Where should I sit?
    {$name}: Just sit in the—
    As you gesture towards the chair, the state that your room is in suddenly hits you. There's a pile of clean clothes on your desk chair that you yet have to put where they belong, a few empty glass bottles that you keep forgetting to throw out, and several books and papers lying on the floor around your bed that you couldn't have been bothered to put away.
    You wince.
    {$name}: Don't say anything.
    {$name}: Just... put the clothes wherever.
    You see Rosinante's lips twitching and you huff.
    {$name}: Sure, laugh at my mortification.
    With a sigh, you continue.
    {$name}: Sorry about the mess.
    Rosinante: You call this a mess? You should see my room.
    He chuckles as he grabs your clothes and places them on your desk before sitting down in the chair.
    Despite your better judgment, a smile pulls on your own lips in return.
    But, your terrible home decor choices didn't bring Rosinante here; you shift a little so that you're facing Rosinante properly, giving him your full attention.
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_TALK_START>>
===

title: date_rosinante_4_TALK_START
location: quarters
---

You wait for a moment, but Rosinante doesn't look eager to start talking. He's sitting in your chair, his hands laid on his lap and playing with the hem of his shirt. He looks... nervous. Like he's scared to tell you what he came for.
-> Wait for him
    You're very curious what's gotten him like this, but it doesn't feel right to push him to talk. And so, you sit quietly, giving him the time he needs.
    It takes a few more seconds of him silently chewing on his bottom lip until he finally opens his mouth to speak.
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_IfDate3>>
-> Prompt him to start talking
    {$name}: So...
    {$name}: What did you want to talk about?
    Rosinante startles, biting on his bottom lip. He mulls over his words for a second longer before finally opening his mouth to speak.
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_IfDate3>>
===

