title: date_rosinante_4_DATE3_FAIL_KIDS
location: quarters
---

You pause, tilting your head to the side, thinking back. He mentioned *something* about it in passing before the two of you made it to the library. Then, before you could ask him about it, he left.
You cringe at the memory; could *that* have gone any worse? You really fucked up there, didn't you?
{$name}: Vaguely... You said that it had everything, I think?
He nods, though his expression darkens. You can't help but wonder whether he's also remembering the bitter memory of that outing.
Rosinante: It does. I wasn't sure I wanted to talk about it with you but—
Rosinante: I'd rather you hear it from *me* than find out through some rumor or something.
You really don't like the way he said it... But after last time, you suppose you can't blame him.
{$name}: You don't have to tell me if you don't want to...
Rosinante shakes his head.
Rosinante: I have to. There's no more running from it.
You frown a little, watching Rosinante as he closes his eyes, visibly preparing for what's to come.
<<jump date_rosinante_4_LOCATION1>>
===

title: date_rosinante_4_DATE3_FAIL_MAPS
location: quarters
---

Of course you do. It seemed to be a really touchy subject for Rosinante.
{$name}: You didn't want to talk about it...
A shadow passes over Rosinante's face.
Rosinante: Yes. And you still pushed.
You cringe at the reminder. You really overstepped there, even though he made it clear where he stood on the topic...
Rosinante: Still, it's partly on me, I overreacted. You...
Rosinante: You deserve an explanation.
{$name}: You don't have to tell me if you don't want to, Rosinante. I'm sorry about earlier, I don't want to force you into telling me.
Rosinante: No, it's OK. I'd rather you hear it from me than some rumor or something.
You tilt your head to the side as Rosinante visibly prepares for what's to come.
<<jump date_rosinante_4_LOCATION2>>
