title: date_rosinante_4_KNEEL
location: quarters
---

Your eyes widen as the reality of the situation sinks in.
You're in the presence of a *Celestial Dragon!* And you've been talking to him so casually... Oh god, what have you done?!
You slide off the bed as fast as you can, immediately dropping to your knees and bowing as deeply as you can.
{$name}: I am deeply sorry for my disrespect up until now. I humbly ask for forgiveness.
There's a moment of silence and you're acutely aware of every breath you take and every beat of your heart.
Rosinante: You can't be serious...
His voice is cold.
Rosinante: I knew telling you would be a mistake.
Rosinante: Get up, stop acting like this. I'm not a Celestial Dragon anymore, nor do I *want* to be.
-> Stay on the ground. You need to show proper respect!
    <<set $rd4_points -=1>>
    {$name}: I cannot do that, my Lord. You are one of the Gods of this land.
    Rosinante goes quiet again and you can feel his burning gaze on you.
    Rosinante: This is beyond ridiculous.
    Rosinante: There's obviously no point talking to you, but don't you dare act this way ever again. Especially in front of other people or I will execute my power—as a *Vice Admiral*—and make sure you never set foot in Marineford again.
    Rosinante: Am I clear?
    You don't dare to look at him when you mumble your agreement.
    {$name}: Understood, sir.
    With a final, disappointed huff, Rosinante gets up from your chair and leaves, stubbing his toe on the way out.
    Well... you definitely messed up. But you couldn't just ignore the fact he's a Celestial Dragon! Still, he sounded really upset.
    You can only hope that you can somehow fix this.
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_DATE_ENDSBad>>
-> Apologize. He sounds upset...
    {$name}: I'm sorry...
    {$name}: I acted on instinct, I didn't mean to be... I don't know, *weird.*
    You sit up, glancing at Rosinante carefully. He looks upset, but he is still the same Rosinante. A marine, a Vice Admiral, a sweet, clumsy man. Why in the world did you do that?
    He sighs, shaking his head.
    Rosinante: It's fine, just...
    Rosinante: Never again.
    {$name}: Of course.
    You climb back on your bed, taking a deep breath before meeting Rosinante's eyes.
    {$name}: Sorry, please continue. I assume it's been a long time since you've lived there?
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_TIMELINE>>
===

title: date_rosinante_4_TEASE
location: quarters
---

It's hard to believe. Rosinante, a Celestial Dragon?
But then, the reality of the situation sinks in. You're in the presence of a *Celestial Dragon!*
You gulp heavily, biting on your bottom lip to keep your expression straight as you shift on your bed to a proper kneeling position. Then, you bow deeply, speaking in the most fake-sincere voice you can possibly muster.
{$name}: I humbly kneel in the presence of a God. I deeply apologize for all reprehensible disrespect I may or may not have shown Your Godliness before today. I am so very honored by Your dazzling presence, oh Saint Rosinante.
A beat of silence passes.
Rosinante: Oh my god, *stop.*
You can hear the anguish in his voice as he whines.
Rosinante: This is really hard for me to talk about, you know. Don't tease me on top of everything...
Finally, you can't hold your amusement in anymore; as a wave of giggles bursts out, you sit up straight once more, giving Rosinante one last cheeky grin.
{$name}: Sorry, I couldn't resist.
{$name}: I'll stop, please continue. I assume it's been a long time since you've lived there?
<<jump date_rosinante_4_TIMELINE>>
===

title: date_rosinante_4_ATTACK
location: quarters
---

{$name}: I can't believe this! I knew the Navy was compliant to what the Celestial Dragons do but to allow one in their ranks?! This is ridiculous!
As you go on with your rant, full of insults and malignance—fueled by anger over the slave survivor stories you've heard, as well as the coldhearted *murder* you've witnessed once before—, Rosinante stays eerily silent.
It's only when you pause to take a breath that he interrupts you, his voice carefully measured.
Rosinante: I knew telling you would be a mistake.
-> {$name}: Yes. It really was.
    {$name}: I've lost all respect for you.
    Rosinante: I see.
    Rosinante: Then I guess we have nothing to talk about.
    His voice is cold as he gets up and turns to leave.
    Rosinante: Respect or not, I am still your superior and this is an order. Do *not* speak to anyone about this or I'll make sure you never set foot in Marineford again.
    Rosinante: Am I clear?
    You take a deep breath, about to snap something back, but something in Rosinante's eyes stops you. You've clearly hurt him.
    Well... Shit.
    You deflate, your eyes dropping to the ground.
    {$name}: Understood.
    With that, Rosinante exits your room, leaving behind heavy silence and a lot of regret.
    You can only hope you can somehow fix this...
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_DATE_ENDSBad>>
-> Suddenly, you realize what you've been saying.
    <<set $rd4_points +=1>>
    *Whom* you've been saying it to. A wave of shame and regret washes over you—after all, Rosinante's never shown anything but kindness and care for other people and you're here, accusing him of crimes someone who merely shared his birthplace committed.
    You take a deep breath, closing your eyes momentarily before you quickly slap your own cheeks.
    When you look at him again a second later, Rosinante looks clearly taken aback by the action.
    {$name}: I'm sorry, I didn't mean to say that. I know you're nothing like *those* people, I just... I don't know.
    {$name}: It wasn't aimed at you. I know you didn't choose where to be born.
    He's silent for a moment, and you gulp heavily. Every second feels like an eternity.
    Finally, he sighs.
    Rosinante: It's fine, I get it. I hate them too.
    You're glad to see he looks a lot more relaxed now than he did just a moment earlier; not so on edge and ready to leave you here with nothing but your own regret.
    You clear your throat awkwardly.
    {$name}: Anyway.
    {$name}: I assume it's been a long time since you've lived there?
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_TIMELINE>>
===

title: date:date_rosinante_4_CONFUSION
location: quarters
---

Rosinante, a Celestial Dragon?
It just sounds... *wrong.*
When you look at Rosinante, you see nothing but kindness and care for other people. You've never met a Celestial Dragon in person but you've heard enough to know they're... none of *that.*
Rosinante: {$name}?
{$name}: Sorry, I'm... trying to wrap my head around this. I mean, this is actually insane.
He doesn't respond.
Nor do you say anything; even so, your mind is racing— and you're sure Rosinante's is doing the same.
{$name}: OK, so...
{$name}: I believe you. But I do feel like this is some fever dream right now.
You laugh a little, and are surprised when Rosinante joins you with his own small chuckle.
Rosinante: It feels like a fever dream talking about this to someone other than Sengoku.
Taking a deep breath, you close your eyes, forcing your swirling thoughts to a stop. You can compute this all later.
{$name}: Sorry, I'm good. Mariejois.
{$name}: I assume it's been a long time since you've lived there?
<<jump date_rosinante_4_TIMELINE>>
===

title: date_rosinante_4_TIMELINE
location: quarters
---

Rosinante: I was six when my family left. We lost the status immediately, too, so I'm not technically a Celestial Dragon anymore either way.
{$name}: That makes sense...
{$name}: And you went to North Blue right after?
Rosinante nods.
Rosinante: We got this large mansion to live in and all. But we lost that pretty soon. People don't take it very well when a disgraced Celestial Dragon starts living in the neighborhood, as you can probably imagine.
He laughs awkwardly, and you wince.
Yeah, you *can* imagine. It wouldn't be pretty, especially for a young child...
{$name}: It must have been terrible...
Rosinante: It was a long time ago. I think it turned out better for me this way, honestly. I can't imagine living in Mariejois my whole life.
{$name}: Don't want to live in a golden cage with Cipher Pol at your every beck and call?
Rosinante: Hell no. Not for a second.
You huff at how immediate and final his answer is. Honestly, you wouldn't expect anything else.
{$name}: Why did you guys leave anyway?
A wistful smile pulls on Rosinante's lips.
Rosinante: My parents thought of themselves as human. They wanted to join ‘normal' people.
{$name}: And they expected that to go well?
He chuckles, but it sounds forced.
Rosinante: Stupid, I know.
-> Yes, incredibly so.
   <<set $rd4_points -=1>>
   <<jump date_rosinante_4_FAMILY_BAD>>
-> Idealistic, more like.
    <<set $rd4_points +=1>>
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_FAMILY_GOOD>>
