title: date_rosinante_4_FAMILY_GOOD
location: quarters
---

{$name}: Not stupid just... naive, I suppose.
{$name}: But they couldn't have known any better since they never had the opportunity to see what the world was like away from the Red Line.
Rosinante: I didn't expect you to say that.
Rosinante: It would be easy to blame them. Doffy certainly did. Or Father at least.
You hum in agreement; you can just imagine Doflamingo reacting to the news... He wasn't called *Heavenly Demon* for nothing after a—wait.
{$name}: Hang on, is this why Doflamingo's called “Heavenly Demon”? Because he was a Celestial Dragon?
Rosinante: I'm honestly not sure. I never asked. But if it's a coincidence, it's one hell of an irony.
Well... You wouldn't put it past someone like Commodore Brannew to think they're so clever coming up with that, but then again, how many people would have known? It would be a complete scandal if something like this became public.
Shaking your head, you focus back at Rosinante.
{$name}: Your parents, what kind of people were they?
Rosinante: They were very kind, both of them. They always tried to do the best for me and Doffy and the people working for us.
{$name}: You mean the slaves.
The words slip through your lips before you can stop yourself.
The smile that appeared on Rosinante's face while he talked about his parents drops immediately and he looks at you with an unreadable expression.
-> Say nothing. You said what you said.
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_SLAVES_NEUTRAL>>
-> Apologize. You didn't mean anything by it.
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_SLAVES_SORRY>>
-> Demand to know how the slaves were treated. You wouldn't stand for injustice.
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_SLAVES_ANGER>>
