title: date_rosinante_4_FAMILY_BAD
location: quarters
---

He clicks his tongue.
Rosinante: Doffy would definitely agree with you. About Father at least.
{$name}: And you don't? You said it yourself.
With a sigh, Rosinante shakes his head.
Rosinante: I mean, yeah. But...
Rosinante: My parents didn't know any better. They lived their whole lives in a gilded cage. How were they supposed to know it would be *that* bad?
Rosinante: They were naive to be sure but—
You frown, tilting your head to the side as you study Rosinante's expression. You're honestly taken aback by what you see—a wistful, sad look.
{$name}: You don't blame them? Not at all?
{$name}: You could have had the most comfortable life and they tossed their children to the wolves because they thought it was a grand adventure or whatever.
He gives you an annoyed look, but you're *right,* OK?
Rosinante: They were the kindest people I've ever known and I'm grateful to them for getting us out.
Rosinante: Sure, the circumstances weren't ideal, mistakes were made. But I'll take it if the alternative is Mariejois.
Rosinante: You know what the place, the people living there are like.
Rosinante: My parents were the exceptions. They were kind, they cared, and they always tried to do the best for me and Doffy *and* the people working for us.
{$name}: You mean the slaves.
The words slip through your lips before you can stop yourself.
Rosinante pauses, the frown on his face deepening the smallest bit as he looks at you with an unreadable expression.
