title: date_rosinante_4_SLAVES_NEUTRAL
location: quarters
---

The both of you are silent for a long while before Rosinante sighs.
Rosinante: There were other servants and security personnel but yes, the slaves too, as messed up as that is.
Rosinante: It's no excuse, but we always treated them well, just like we would any other person. I probably wouldn't be able to live with myself today otherwise...
-> {$name}: I know.
    {$name}: You're a very kind person, just like your parents. I can't imagine you doing anything bad to anyone.
    {$name}: Can't say the same about Doflamingo but...
    Rosinante laughs a little and you're relieved.
    Rosinante: Thank you. I'm glad you think so.
    Warmth envelops you as your eyes meet Rosinante's soft gaze.
    {$name}: Of course.
    <<set $rd4_points +=1>>
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_CLOSURE_GOOD>>
-> {$name}: That can't be true.
    {$name}: No Celestial Dragon is capable of seeing their slaves as human.
    {$name}: Just look how they act! At the human auctions in Sabaody! Or how Doflamingo turned out!
    Rosinante: I'm not my brother.
    Rosinante: And neither were our parents. They've never done one bad thing to any of their people.
    His voice is cold. You've definitely upset him...
    <<set $rd4_points -=1>>
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_CLOSURE_BAD>>
===

title: date_rosinante_4_SLAVES_SORRY
location: quarters
---

{$name}: I'm sorry, I didn't mean anything by it! Your parents sound lovely, I'm sure they didn't even have slaves!
Rosinante sighs, and you feel like there's a tinge of disappointment in there...
Rosinante: You're overdoing it. Of course we had slaves while still in Mariejois. We treated them well, of course, though that's no excuse.
Rosinante: There's no way we *wouldn't* have any. I'm sure you know that.
Rosinante: So stop, please.
You gulp. How much more obvious could you have made it that you're scared to say the wrong thing? Damn it...
{$name}: Yes, I'm sorry...
<<jump date_rosinante_4_CLOSURE_NEUTRAL>>
===

title: date_rosinante_4_SLAVES_ANGER
location: quarters
---

You can't help the way your stomach turns at the very idea of anyone ‘owning' slaves. You have to ask, you *have to*... But you're not so sure you'll be able to keep the hostility out of your voice...
{$name}: You had slaves, didn't you? How did you treat them?
*Good enough.* Hopefully.
If Rosinante hears your anger and disgust, he doesn't show it.
Rosinante: We treated them well, just like any other person. Even Doffy never did or said anything to them, our mom made sure of it.
-> Believe him. Rosinante wouldn't lie about this.
    You nod with a smile, and Rosinante gives you a teasing grin in return.
    Rosinante: I'm glad you were worried about them. I get where you're coming from, the slave market is disgusting...
    Oops.
    Yeah, he definitely could hear something from your tone.
    {$name}: I had to make sure, OK?
    You defend yourself with a small laugh, relieved.
    <<set $rd4_points +=1>>
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_CLOSURE_GOOD>>
-> Don't believe him. There's no way he'd admit it.
    You narrow your eyes at him.
    {$name}: Why should I believe you?
    Rosinante lets out a short bark of laughter. He doesn't sound very happy or amused though.
    Rosinante: I get where you're coming from, the slave market is disgusting.
    Rosinante: So, if nothing else, I'm glad you're worried about the people.
    He gives you a crooked smile.
    -> Admit defeat.
        With a huff, you finally nod.
        {$name}: OK, I get it. I trust you.
        Rosinante: Thank you.
        <<jump date_rosinante_4_CLOSURE_NEUTRAL>>
    -> Still don't believe him.
        <<set $rd4_points -=1>>
        {$name}: You didn't answer me.
        Rosinante: You have nothing but my word, I don't know what else to tell you.
        Rosinante: If you can't trust me, then I think the discussion's completely pointless, don't you think?
        You can't say you're happy with his answer, but he sounds annoyed. And well, he's right. There's nothing to talk about.
        <<jump date_rosinante_4_CLOSURE_BAD>>
===

title: date_rosinante_4_CLOSURE_GOOD
location: quarters
---

The two of you exchange a smile. A moment passes in comfortable silence, a silence full of understanding, trust, and warmth. You couldn't be more grateful that Rosinante has chosen to confide in you.
Finally, Rosinante clears his throat.
Rosinante: Anyway...
Rosinante: Now when you read the name Donquixote in history books, you'll know who we are.
Rosinante: Thank you for hearing me out, {$name}.
You shake your head with a small huff.
{$name}: Thank *you* for trusting me with this. I won't tell a soul.
His smile widens, but suddenly, there's also this uncertain look in his eyes.
Rosinante: Does what I told you change anything? Between us, I mean.
Rosinante: Wait, that sounded wrong.
Rosinante: I mean, do you see me differently, knowing my past?
-> No.
    <<set $rd4_points +=2>>
    You can't help the giggle that bubbles out of his chest at the way he waves his arms around. You're half-expecting him to fall off the chair any second now.
    {$name}: Of course not. You're still you, Rosinante.
    The smile he gives you this time is so bright that it almost blinds you and something stirs in your stomach at the sight.
    Before you can say anything more, a huge, embarrassing yawn escapes you.
    Rosinante chuckles and gets up. As he wishes you good night with one final grin—but not before accidentally knocking the pile of clothes on your desk to the ground—, you finally fall into your pillows once more.
    It was an exhausting conversation, especially on top of everything that's happened earlier in the day... But, you haven't felt this good, this *happy* in a while.
    You can't wait to talk to Rosinante again.
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_BEST_ENDING>>
-> Maybe.
    <<set $rd4_points +=1>>
    {$name}: To be honest... I'm not sure.
    {$name}: I don't *think* so but... It's a lot.
    Rosinante smiles, but there's a little sadness behind it.
    Rosinante: I know. And I dropped it on you so suddenly too.
    He laughs awkwardly and you shake your head.
    {$name}: Not at all, don't worry! I just need to sleep on it to process it, that's all.
    {$name}: I'll be full insubordination mode with you by tomorrow, I'm sure.
    He laughs at your joke, and a wave of relief washes over you. Yeah, you'll definitely stop feeling weird about this by morning. You won't be able to stay away from that laugh for long if you try.
    Suddenly, a huge, embarrassing yawn escapes you.
    {$name}: Sorry, I think this is it for me for tonight...
    With one last chuckle, Rosinante gets up from the chair and, wishing you good night, leaves you alone with your pillow once more—though not before accidentally knocking the pile of clothes on your desk to the ground.
    It was an exhausting conversation, especially on top of everything that's happened earlier in the day... But, you haven't felt this good, this *happy* in a while.
    You can't wait to talk to Rosinante again.
    <<jump date_rosinante_4_GOOD_Ending>>
===

title: date_rosinante_4_CLOSURE_NEUTRAL
location: quarters
---

A moment of silence passes between you; it's not uncomfortable, just the type of silence where everything that needed to be said has been said.
Finally, Rosinante clears his throat.
Rosinante: Well, that's it. That's where I come from and why it's hard for me to talk about.
Rosinante: Now when you see the name Donquixote in history books, you'll know who we are.
{$name}: I get it. Thank you for telling me.
Rosinante: No problem.
Rosinante: Just... Don't—
{$name}: Tell anyone. I know, I promise.
Rosinante: Thank you, {$name}.
You smile, but then frown slightly when you notice the uncertain look in Rosinante's eyes.
{$name}: Rosinante?
Rosinante: I know it's been a lot but... I hope it doesn't change how you see me.
{$name}: Well... it's going to take a bit to process for sure...
Rosinante: Right...
{$name}: But I'll be fine.
He sighs in relief, giving you a small smile.
Rosinante: That's good to hear.
Rosinante: I shouldn't keep you up any longer, please get some rest, {$name}.
With that, Rosinante gets up from the chair and, wishing you good night, leaves you alone with your pillow once more—though not before accidentally knocking the pile of clothes on your desk to the ground.
As you let yourself fall face first into the pillow with a huge yawn, you feel the exhaustion from the conversation, and the day as a whole, set in.
Taking a deep breath, you decide to think about all this tomorrow. Right now, you don't have the capacity to process it all.
<<jump date_rosinante_4_NEUTRAL_ENDING>>
===

title:
location: quarters
---

Uncomfortable silence settles over your room. You're pretty sure this talk couldn't have gone any worse than it did without Rosinante getting up and leaving in the middle.
What can you say? *Is* there anything to say?
Finally, Rosinante clears his throat. Even that simple sound is strained.
Rosinante: Well, that's it. My birthplace, and the truth about the Donquixote family.
Rosinante: It's clear you're not thrilled about it but that's how it is. At least you heard it from me.
Rosinante: I'm not going to ask you to treat me the same, but I *do* ask you don't tell anyone about this for obvious reasons.
{$name}: Understood.
With that, Rosinante gets up from the chair and, wishing you good night, leaves you alone with your pillow once more—though not before accidentally knocking the pile of clothes on your desk to the ground.
As you let yourself fall face first into the pillow with a huge yawn, you feel the exhaustion from the conversation, and the day as a whole, set in.
It wasn't a pretty listen, it wasn't a good conversation... But maybe, you should have been more understanding.
There's nothing you can do about it now, is there?
<<jump date_rosinante_4_BAD_ENDING>>
===

